# mention — reference an issue and a skill with `@`, then let the agent go.
#
# The picker is the demo, so the take is mostly typing: `@` opens on files, Tab walks to GitHub,
# a filter finds the issue, Enter makes it a chip; then `@` again for a skill. Sending it is the
# last beat, and the take ends once the agent has visibly picked both up.
#
# The repository is fictional, so `gh` is a stand-in (`gh/gh`) that answers for `acme/todo` and
# refuses anything else. Everything else is real, including the model reading the issue it was
# pointed at.

#: cols 120
#: rows 32
#: speed 1.0
#: model anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5
#: thinking medium
#: glyphs nerd
#: bin gh
#: seed bash "$DEMO_SCRIPTS/demo-skills.sh"
#: setup git remote add origin https://github.com/acme/todo.git

answer Return hold 3 when Allow once
answer Return hold 3.5 when Enter submit

sleep 3
mark start
sleep 1

type fix
key space
sleep 0.3
type @
sleep 1.6

log walk the tabs to GitHub
key Tab
sleep 1.6
key Tab
expect #12 max 20
sleep 2.2

log narrow to the issue and insert it
type miss
sleep 1.8
key Return
sleep 1.2

type with
key space
sleep 0.3
type @
sleep 1.2
key Tab
sleep 1.0
type test
sleep 1.6
key Return
sleep 1.8

log send it
key Return

log the agent reads both
settle 5 max 240
sleep 2.5
mark end
